If a monster egg is 150-200 moves old, and is in your inventory
(not in a sack), there is a chance it will hatch.  If it it over
200 turns old, and in your inventory, it will turn from a monster
egg to an ordinary egg.

So, if you lay an gray dragon egg, wait 200 moves, then pick it up,
it will turn into a normal egg.  Similarly, if you keep it in a
bag for 200 moves, and then take it out, it will turn into a normal
egg.

If you pick it up as soon as you lay it, and then keep it in your 
inventory (but not in a bag), it will probably hatch in 150-200 moves.
There is a chance that it will "go bad", and turn into a normal egg 
after 200 moves.  (I'd guess 80-90% chance of hatching).
